From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: appxpackaging: add the AppX/MSIX package reader

Wine had no appxpackaging.dll, so CoCreateInstance of AppxFactory and
AppxBundleFactory failed with REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG. winget reads its
community source -- an MSIX package -- through them, as do installers and
package tools.

Add the DLL with IAppxFactory (package and manifest readers) and
IAppxBundleFactory, which tells a bundle from a package the way callers
expect (APPX_E_MISSING_REQUIRED_FILE); reading bundles themselves is not
implemented yet. The package reader is a bounds-checked ZIP/ZIP64 reader with
inflate, the manifest reader (identity, properties, applications with their
VisualElements, capabilities, OS prerequisites; xmllite with DTDs prohibited)
and IAppxManifestPackageId with full and family names.

The block map is enforced as on Windows: the archive and AppxBlockMap.xml must
list the same files at the same sizes or the package is refused
(APPX_E_INVALID_BLOCKMAP), and every payload file and the manifest is checked
block by block against its hashes when read (APPX_E_BLOCK_HASH_INVALID). The
package signature covers the block map, so this is what makes a signature
cover the payload. Also: IAppxFile streams, payload enumeration, content types
from [Content_Types].xml, SHA-256/384/512 block maps.

Gate: test/appx-gate.sh (fixtures from test/mkappx.py).

